course: dictionary
lesson: 5615
title: One word, many meanings: lightly
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and context tells you which one fits. Lightly means with little force or weight, as in «tap lightly». It can also mean a little, as in «lightly salted», or not seriously, as in «take something lightly». Read the words around it to decide.
explain: Look at the clues. «The moment the key turns, Toad hops lightly out of bed» is about movement: he moves quietly and without fuss, so lightly means gently and softly. In a recipe, «lightly beat the eggs» means not too hard. Always ask: what would fit here? Then swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: «Don't take this lightly» is not about weight at all. It means do not treat it as unimportant. The same word can mean something quite different in each sentence, so the clues around it matter more than the word alone.
fact: Lightly means with little force or weight, as in «tap lightly».
fact: Lightly can also mean a little, as in «lightly cooked».
fact: «Take something lightly» means not treating it as serious or worrying.
fact: «Get off lightly» means having only a small punishment.
fact: «Sleep lightly» means not sleeping very deeply, so you wake easily.
exercise: «The moment the key turns, Toad hops lightly out of bed.» What does lightly mean here? | *Gently and quietly, with little weight or noise | Slowly, like a sleepy snail | Very loudly, banging the bed | Angrily, stamping his feet
exercise: Dad says, «Don't take this lightly.» What does he mean? | This is light, so pick it up | *This is serious, so treat it with care | This is cheap to buy | This is funny, so laugh about it
exercise: A recipe says «lightly beat the eggs». What does lightly suggest? | *Not too hard, just enough to mix | For a very long time | As hard as you can | Without using any eggs at all
test: «Artists lightly sketch big simple shapes first.» What does lightly mean here? | Not at all, so they skip it | Loudly and with a lot of force | *Only a little, with faint light lines | Very darkly, in thick black ink
test: The cook says, «The fish is lightly salted.» What does lightly mean? | Covered in a thick layer of salt | Washed in sea water | Not salted at all | *Only a little bit of salt
exam: «He will get off lightly.» What does this mean? | He will be lost in the town | He will be punished a lot | He will be famous for his work | *He will have only a small punishment
